  "grammar_observation": {
    "target_language": "Mae gan Sam gacen. Mae gan Sam bapur. Mae gan Dafi bensil. Oes gan Dafi bensil? Ond: does gan Dafi ddim pensil. Mae gen i gacen.",
    "bridge_language": "Welsh expresses possession with gan. In this pattern, an indefinite thing possessed soft-mutates in a positive statement or question (cacen → gacen, papur → bapur, pensil → bensil); ddim blocks that mutation in a negative. Use gen i for “I have”."
  },
